## The console's Caddy block (zylos/README.md "The Caddy block"). Lines
## starting with ## are notes and are left out by `node zylos/lib.js caddy`,
## which prints the block with this host's values in place of <NAME>,
## <BASE_PATH>, <PORT>, <USERS_FILE> and <USER_HEADER>. Paste the printed
## block inside the primary site block of ~/zylos/http/Caddyfile, just
## before its closing }, keeping the BEGIN/END lines (zylos uninstall
## removes the block by them).
##
## - handle_path strips <BASE_PATH>: the console's links are all relative.
## - The public Host is passed through unchanged (no `header_up Host`): the
##   console compares Origin with Host, and answers only a Host named by
##   --allow-host (console.allow_host_key).
## - basic_auth answers 401 first; `request_header -<USER_HEADER>` drops any
##   copy the visitor sent; `header_up <USER_HEADER>` sets the logged-in user.
# BEGIN zylos-component:<NAME>
redir <BASE_PATH> <BASE_PATH>/ permanent
handle_path <BASE_PATH>/* {
    basic_auth {
        import <USERS_FILE>
    }
    request_header -<USER_HEADER>
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:<PORT> {
        header_up <USER_HEADER> {http.auth.user.id}
    }
}
# END zylos-component:<NAME>
